/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 45 0 R
/T (1. Objective The goal of this assignment is to implement a 3-bit counter driven by a 1 Hz clock signal. The clock originates from the FPGA's internal oscillator, is fed into a Phase-Locked Loop \(PLL\) that generates an 8 MHz output clock, and is then divided down to 1 Hz using a clock divider module. Running the counter at such a slow clock rate allows its state transitions to be observed visually on the on-board FPGA LEDs.)
/E (1. Objective The goal of this assignment is to implement a 3-bit counter driven by a 1 Hz clock signal. The clock originates from the FPGA's internal oscillator, is fed into a Phase-Locked Loop \(PLL\) that generates an 8 MHz output clock, and is then divided down to 1 Hz using a clock divider module. Running the counter at such a slow clock rate allows its state transitions to be observed visually on the on-board FPGA LEDs.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
