152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (shows the input clock \(clk\), the active-low reset chain \(rst_n, pll_rst\), the 8 MHz PLL output \(pll_clk\), the divided clock \(div_clk\), and the resulting 3-bit counter value. Note on simulation clock rate: the final design divides the 8 MHz PLL clock down to 1 Hz for real-time observation of the LEDs on the actual board. However, simulating a full 1 Hz period in a behavioral testbench would require simulating on the order of seconds of real time, which translates into a very large number of simulation cycles and an impractically long run time / waveform database. For this reason, the clock-divider parameters were temporarily scaled up for simulation purposes only, so that div_clk toggles at 1 MHz instead of 1 Hz. This keeps the functional behavior identical \(the counter still increments once per div_clk rising edge and wraps modulo 8\) while keeping the simulation time manageable. The actual hardware implementation still uses the 1 Hz divide ratio described in Section 5.2. 7.1 Waveform \(Simulated at 1 MHz\))
/E (shows the input clock \(clk\), the active-low reset chain \(rst_n, pll_rst\), the 8 MHz PLL output \(pll_clk\), the divided clock \(div_clk\), and the resulting 3-bit counter value. Note on simulation clock rate: the final design divides the 8 MHz PLL clock down to 1 Hz for real-time observation of the LEDs on the actual board. However, simulating a full 1 Hz period in a behavioral testbench would require simulating on the order of seconds of real time, which translates into a very large number of simulation cycles and an impractically long run time / waveform database. For this reason, the clock-divider parameters were temporarily scaled up for simulation purposes only, so that div_clk toggles at 1 MHz instead of 1 Hz. This keeps the functional behavior identical \(the counter still increments once per div_clk rising edge and wraps modulo 8\) while keeping the simulation time manageable. The actual hardware implementation still uses the 1 Hz divide ratio described in Section 5.2. 7.1 Waveform \(Simulated at 1 MHz\))
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (As shown in the waveform, once the PLL locks and the reset is released, the 8 MHz pll_clk toggles continuously, and div_clk produces one pulse per divider period \(1 MHz in this simulation run\). The counter[2:0] value increments synchronously with div_clk and correctly wraps around from 7 \(111\) back to 0 \(000\), confirming proper 3-bit modulo-8 counting behavior. The same logic behavior is expected at the real 1 Hz operating rate on hardware.)
/E (As shown in the waveform, once the PLL locks and the reset is released, the 8 MHz pll_clk toggles continuously, and div_clk produces one pulse per divider period \(1 MHz in this simulation run\). The counter[2:0] value increments synchronously with div_clk and correctly wraps around from 7 \(111\) back to 0 \(000\), confirming proper 3-bit modulo-8 counting behavior. The same logic behavior is expected at the real 1 Hz operating rate on hardware.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
