360 0 obj
<<
/Title (shows the input clock \(clk\), the active-low reset chain \(rst_n, pll_rst\), the 8 MHz PLL output \(pll_clk\), the divided clock \(div_clk\), and the resulting 3-bit counter value. Note on simulation clock rate: the final design divides the 8 MHz PLL clock down to 1 Hz for real-time observation of the LEDs on the actual board. However, simulating a full 1 Hz period in a behavioral testbench would require simulating on the order of seconds of real time, which translates into a very large number of simulation cycles and an impractically long run time / waveform database. For this reason, the clock-divider parameters were temporarily scaled up for simulation purposes only, so that div_clk toggles at 1 MHz instead of 1 Hz. This keeps the functional behavior identical \(the counter still increments once per div_clk rising edge and wraps modulo 8\) while keeping the simulation time manageable. The actual hardware implementation still uses the 1 Hz divide ratio described in Section 5.2. 7.1 Waveform \(Simulated at 1 MHz\))
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 181 0 R
/Prev 280 0 R
/Next 403 0 R
>>
endobj
