403 0 obj
<<
/Title (As shown in the waveform, once the PLL locks and the reset is released, the 8 MHz pll_clk toggles continuously, and div_clk produces one pulse per divider period \(1 MHz in this simulation run\). The counter[2:0] value increments synchronously with div_clk and correctly wraps around from 7 \(111\) back to 0 \(000\), confirming proper 3-bit modulo-8 counting behavior. The same logic behavior is expected at the real 1 Hz operating rate on hardware.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 181 0 R
/Prev 360 0 R
/Next 404 0 R
>>
